title: $:/tiddlyrpg/language/en-GB/Check/

Checks/Unknown: Check the fields: $field$ names "$id$", which is no check
Dates/Beyond: Check the text: <<date $n$>> - the field date has $count$ sections
Dates/Day: Check the date: $point$ - day $day$ does not exist in month $month$ of $year$
Dates/EmptySection: Check the date: an empty section (two commas in a row)
Dates/EmptySide: Check the date: an empty side in "$section$"
Dates/Forever: Check the date: it starts with ".." - there since time immemorial?
Dates/Head: Check the event: text before the first <<date>>
Dates/Month: Check the date: $point$ - month $month$ does not exist
Dates/NoDate: Check the event: it has no date
Dates/NoHeading: Check the event: no <<date>> for section $sections$
Dates/NoPlaceholder: Check the event: every event starts with <<date>>
Dates/OpenPhase: Check the date: the phase $section$ has no end, but a later one follows
Dates/Order: Check the date: $section$ comes before the section ahead of it
Dates/Rule: Check the text: "---" right before <<date>> of section $n$ - the heading draws its own rule
Dates/StartAfterEnd: Check the date: $section$ - the start is after the end
Dates/Twice: Check the text: two <<date>> for section $n$
Dates/Unreadable: Check the date: cannot read $parts$
Expected/Image: Check the fields: no image yet (field image)
Expected/Map: Check the fields: no map yet (field map)
Expected/Player: Check the fields: who plays this character? (field player)
Expected/Text: Check the text: it has no text yet
Fields/Reserved: Check the definition: $field$ is a field of the core or of a relation - name it otherwise
Fields/Twice: Check the definition: $field$ is defined in $other$ already
Fields/Undefined: Check the schema: $field$ has no definition
Images/Image: Check the image: $path$ does not exist
Images/Joined: Check the spot: $spot$ is joined to $target$ - its images and maps show there, set them in that tiddler
Images/Macro: Check the text: <<image>> shows $path$, which does not exist
Images/Map: Check the map: $path$ does not exist
Images/NoFolder: Check the text: <<image "$files$">> in a tiddler without type - name the folder, e.g. folder:"event"
Images/SpotImage: Check the spot $spot$: its image $path$ does not exist
Images/SpotMap: Check the spot $spot$: its map $path$ does not exist
Images/Unused: Check the file: no tiddler shows it - use it in image, map or <<image>>, or remove it
Links/Missing: Check the link: $target$ does not exist - create it, unlink it or leave it on purpose
Links/MissingOften: Check the link: $target$ does not exist and is linked from $count$ tiddlers - create it, unlink it or leave it on purpose
Links/MissingSpot: Check the link: $target$ is no tiddler, only a spot of $place$ - link it with <<spotlink "$place$" "$target$">>, or create the tiddler
Locations/Tag: Check the tags: $tag$ is a location - locations are never tags, the place goes into the field location
Plugins/ExtensionBase: Check the extension: there is no domain $domain$ to extend
Plugins/ExtensionId: Check the extension: $domain$ has "$id$" already
Plugins/ExtensionType: Check the extension: $domain$ is of type $type$; only label domains can be extended
Plugins/Reference: Check the currency: the coin of the prices of the ruleset is $reference$, which is none of its coins ($coins$)
Plugins/TraitCycle: Check the domain $domain$: "$id$" is its own ancestor
Plugins/TraitFor: Check the domain $domain$: "$id$" belongs to "$parent$", which is no entry of it
Plugins/disabled: Check the choice: $configured$ is disabled - active is $active$
Plugins/missing: Check the choice: $configured$ is not installed - active is $active$
Plugins/type: Check the choice: $configured$ is no plugin of this type - active is $active$
Quests/NoMarker: Check the quest: it has no marker yet - mark it in an event: <<quest "$name$">>
Quests/SimilarQuest: Check the name: it is close to the quest $other$ - one quest written two ways?
Quests/SimilarRumour: Check the name: it is close to the rumour $other$ - one quest written two ways?
Relations/Ancestor: Check the family: the line of parents already reaches the ancestor $other$
Relations/DeadLeader: Check the fields: dead, and $successors$ leads $target$ already - the dead one is a member of it now (member instead of leader)
Relations/DeadLeaderPlace: Check the fields: dead, and $successors$ leads $target$ already - remove $target$ from leader
Relations/Family: Check the family: family names $other$, who is already parent, ancestor, spouse or sibling
Relations/Former: Check the fields: $field$ and former both name $target$ - it is one of them
Relations/Included: Check the fields: $field$ names $target$, whom $other$ already includes
Relations/Leaders: Check the organisation: several lead it ($leaders$) - a council, or one too many?
Relations/Missing: Check the field $field$: $target$ does not exist
Relations/MissingSpot: Check the field $field$: $target$ is no tiddler, only a spot of $place$ - a tiddler named $target$ joins the spot
Relations/Siblings: Check the family: $other$ is a child of $parent$ too, but no sibling - true siblings, half siblings or on purpose?
Relations/Symmetric: Check the field $field$: $other$ names this tiddler, here $other$ is missing
Secrets/Transclusion: Check the text: it transcludes the secret tiddler $target$ - every view that sees this tiddler sees it
Secrets/View: Check the text: it asks the view itself - lock with the tag Secret, <<secret>> or <$secret>
Spots/JoinedText: Check the spot: $spot$ is joined to a tiddler - the text of the spot shows only here, move it into the tiddler $target$
Spots/Similar: Check the spot: $spot$ is close to the tiddler $title$ - a typo? With the same name the spot joins it
Types/Missing: Check the tags: no type tag (person, location, event, ...) - it shows in no hub
